From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:44:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: Add an owned stream type for response bodies

A response body is today held twice: as a state in a shared
`Arc<Mutex<ResponseBody>>` and as a `done_chan` that every fetch function
passes along by `&mut`. The consumer's half of that channel keeps a sender
clone, so a producer that exits without sending `Done` hangs its consumer.

Add `net_traits::body_stream`: a single-producer stream of chunks that ends
in exactly one `BodyEnd` (complete, aborted, or failed with a network
error). The producer owns the only `BodySender`, so if it returns, panics
or is dropped without finishing, the receiver ends the body as failed
instead of waiting. `BodyReceiver::read_all` implements "fully read".

Nothing uses it yet; the next patch replaces `done_chan` with it.

Validation: `./mach test-unit -p servo-net-traits`: 104 tests pass, among them the 8 new ones in tests/body_stream.rs. Negative control: with a closed channel ending the body as complete, `test_body_without_finish_fails` and `test_body_of_a_panicking_producer_fails` fail.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; the agent wrote the type and its tests following docs/fetch-body-stream-plan-2026-10-22.md in the workspace)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
